{"step_index":167,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T10:46:59Z","thinking":"**Verifying System Route Status**\n\nAll routes return 200 OK, indicating successful endpoint operation. Now shifting focus to generating the `walkthrough.md` file, aiming to encapsulate the agent's actions and thought process. This artifact will document the executed changes comprehensively.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Detailed walkthrough of the NEXUS AI-powered criminal network analysis dashboard frontend implementation and verification results.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# NEXUS // Criminal Network Analysis Intelligence Dashboard\n\nNEXUS is an AI-powered criminal network analysis frontend designed for law enforcement and intelligence task forces. Built with React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, React Router, and tactical UI primitives inspired by Palantir Gotham, Analyst's Notebook, and Maltego.\n\n---\n\n## Workspace Location\nThe complete frontend project has been created and verified at:\n`C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`\n\n---\n\n## Key Features & Completed Pages\n\n### 1. Login (`/login`)\n- **Law-Enforcement Gate**: Title 18 U.S.C. § 1030 warning header with real-time AES-256 link status.\n- **Officer Credentials**: Badge ID (`FED-8491`), encrypted hardware token PIN, and division selector (Transnational Crime, Cyber Warfare, Anti-Money Laundering, INTERPOL).\n- **Biometric Simulation**: Live hardware token validation sequence.\n- **Evaluation Profiles**: One-click quick-login triggers for \"Lead Investigator Sarah Vance\" and \"SIGINT Analyst\".\n\n### 2. Dashboard (`/`)\n- **Command Center Telemetry**: Real-time status indicators with DEFCON-3 alert badge and sector telemetry.\n- **Tactical KPI Metric Cards**:\n  - *Active High-Value Targets* (42 HVTs with sparkline)\n  - *Tracked Illicit Financial Flow* ($148.6M across 16 jurisdictions)\n  - *Live Intercept Feeds* (189 active feeds)\n  - *AI Anomaly Threat Index* (84.2 with neural recalculation)\n- **Embedded Network Topology Radar**: Live interactive canvas showing the active criminal syndicate cluster for *Operation Phantom Web*.\n- **Priority Intercept Stream**: Triage alert feed with AI confidence metrics, source identifiers (SIGINT, FINCEN, ANPR), and plot actions.\n- **Active Operations Table**: Multi-jurisdictional case table with sorting, search, and status pills.\n\n### 3. Cases & Warrants (`/cases`)\n- **Case Management**: Filter by status (*Active Investigation*, *Interdiction Imminent*, *Surveillance Phase*, *Grand Jury*) and priority (*CRITICAL*, *HIGH*, *MEDIUM*).\n- **Operational Metrics**: Aggregated warrants issued, seized asset values ($123.5M), and active target counts.\n- **Case Dossier Inspection**: Detailed drawer showing case charters, lead agents, jurisdiction, and linked suspects.\n- **Interactive Charter Issuance**: Modal to launch new operations with tactical codenames and AI auto-tagging.\n\n### 4. Upload Evidence (`/upload`)\n- **Ingestion Vault**: Multi-format support for Call Detail Records (CDR), SWIFT wire ledgers, VoLTE audio intercepts, ANPR video, and forensic disk images.\n- **Automated SHA-256 Hashing**: Generates Title 18 compliant immutable checksums with instant clipboard copy.\n- **Chain of Custody Protocol**: Custodial officer name, badge number, and GPS collection location.\n- **4-Stage AI Pipeline Visualizer**:\n  1. *SHA-256 Checksum Verification*\n  2. *Named Entity Recognition (NER)*\n  3. *Biometric & Voiceprint Matching*\n  4. *Topology Graph Vectorization*\n- **Verified Archive Binder**: Live cards showing ingested items with inspection modals for raw intercept payloads.\n\n### 5. Network Analysis Workbench (`/network`)\n- **Full-Screen Interactive Topology**:\n  - Zoom in/out, pan, reset view, and zoom percentage indicator.\n  - Multi-node classification: Suspects (red), Shell Companies (amber), Burner Phones (cyan), Bank Accounts (emerald), Safehouses (purple), Vehicles (sky blue).\n  - Relationship vectors: Wire transfers with money pill badges, encrypted VoLTE calls (dashed), co-conspirators, and courier links.\n  - Filter Drawer: Threat score slider (0-95+), entity class toggles, and suspicious transfer highlights.\n  - Node Inspector Drawer: Degree centrality, betweenness score, legal status, direct vectors, and one-click pivot to full dossier.\n  - **Shortest Attribution Pathfinder**: Calculates shortest network path between targets (e.g. Viktor Ramos ➔ Elena Rostova ➔ Aethelgard Holdings ➔ Zurich Credit Union).\n  - Graph export options (JSON, Gephi bundle).\n\n### 6. Entity Profile Dossier (`/entity/:id`)\n- **Target Intelligence Dossier**:\n  - High-Value Target header with tactical photo/mugshot, wanted charges, calculated threat index (e.g. 96/100), and last known GPS coordinates with timestamp.\n  - Quick target switcher strip to jump between syndicate members.\n  - Tabbed intelligence views:\n    - *Overview*: Biographical data, aliases, weapons, biometrics, active charges.\n    - *Network Associates*: Direct co-conspirators with connection weights and risk ratings.\n    - *Financial Footprint*: Structured offshore wires and layering breakdown.\n    - *Intercepted Comms*: Transcribed Title-III intercepts and VoLTE recordings.\n    - *Evidence Vault*: Directly linked cryptographic evidence items.\n    - *AI Threat Evaluation*: LLM synthesis of flight risk (92.4%), asset dissipation risk, and tactical interdiction recommendations.\n\n### 7. Investigation Timeline (`/timeline`)\n- **Chronological Intelligence Stream**: Chronological event correlation with custom icon bullets for wiretaps, financial transfers, border crossings, raids, and comms.\n- **Filter Controls**: Filter by event category and target entity correlation.\n- **Corroboration Confidence**: AI confidence rating on each timeline event with direct links to cryptographic evidence references.\n- **Event Inspection Modal**: Drill down into event context, participants, and timestamp data.\n\n### 8. System Settings (`/settings`)\n- **AI Neural Parameters**:\n  - Financial anomaly sensitivity slider\n  - Facial recognition match confidence slider\n  - Autonomous graph edge creation toggle\n  - Voiceprint acoustic clustering toggle\n- **Interface & Themes**:\n  - One-click toggle between Tactical Dark Mode and Analytical Light Mode.\n  - Data density toggles and classification watermarking.\n- **Officer Credentials & Security**:\n  - FIDO2 hardware token status, clearance level (Level 5 Alpha), and session countdown.\n- **CJIS Audit Log**:\n  - Immutable activity log with timestamped entries and SHA-256 signatures.\n\n---\n\n## Reusable Components Implemented\n\n| Component | Path | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Sidebar** | [Sidebar.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx) | Collapsible tactical sidebar with classification badge, active mission pill, and live route counters |\n| **TopNav** | [TopNav.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/layout/TopNav.tsx) | Global intelligence search, classification banner, theme toggle, and alert dropdown |\n| **MetricCard** | [MetricCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/MetricCard.tsx) | KPI cards with dynamic sparkline SVGs, trend indicators, and severity glow borders |\n| **DataTable** | [DataTable.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/DataTable.tsx) | Generic sortable, searchable, paginated tactical table component |\n| **NetworkGraphContainer** | [NetworkGraphContainer.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/network/NetworkGraphContainer.tsx) | Interactive SVG network graph with pan, zoom, node selection, edge labeling, and filtering |\n| **EvidenceCard** | [EvidenceCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/EvidenceCard.tsx) | Evidence cards with SHA-256 copy, file format badges, and raw intercept modal |\n| **EntityCard** | [EntityCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/EntityCard.tsx) | Suspect cards with threat gauge, aliases, GPS location, and graph plot actions |\n| **AlertCard** | [AlertCard.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Nityam%20Jaiswal/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nexus/src/components/common/AlertCard.tsx) | Operational alert cards with AI confidence meter, source tag, and triage actions |\n\n---\n\n## Verification Results\n\n### Build Verification\n- Executed `npm run build`:\n  - `tsc -b` passed with 0 errors.\n  - `vite build` completed in **788ms**.\n  - Generated assets: `dist/index.html` (1.28 kB), `dist/assets/index.css` (37.84 kB), `dist/assets/index.js` (421.70 kB).\n\n### Live Server & Route HTTP Verification\n- Vite development server started at `http://localhost:5173/`.\n- Tested all 8 routes via automated HTTP requests:\n  - `GET /` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /login` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /cases` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /upload` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /network` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /entity/ent-1` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /timeline` ➔ **200 OK**\n  - `GET /settings` ➔ **200 OK**\n","Description":"Create walkthrough.md documentation for NEXUS dashboard","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fb69bf55-26d8-4420-a8a5-e461b2943c07\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Creating walkthrough artifact","toolSummary":"Create walkthrough.md"}}]}
